    <string name="in_app_rules_title">In-app rules</string>
    <string name="in_app_rules_info_title">In-app rules</string>
    <string name="in_app_rules_info_body">In-app rules apply only to the selected profile.\n\nChoose a mode:\n• Block selected: Only selected sections are blocked.\n• Allow selected: Selected sections stay available; other supported sections of that app are blocked.\n\nStatus:\n• Available: Supported for the installed app version.\n• Experimental: May vary by app version, language, entry point, or device.\n• Disabled: The app is not installed or the rule cannot currently be used.\n• Coming soon: Planned, but not yet enforceable.\n\nLoq In detects these sections using Accessibility. For YouTube Shorts, 2.2.5 combines navigation state, screen geometry and multiple Accessibility text/content-description signals instead of relying on a single internal view ID. Short delayed re-checks help when YouTube loads controls asynchronously. Changes to supported apps can still affect detection.\n\nYouTube Shorts can use two layers together: Loq In keeps its own Shorts detection and blocking active, while YouTube’s native Settings → Time management → Shorts feed limit → 0 can add a second layer. Loq In also recognizes the native limit-reached screen as an additional high-confidence Shorts signal. The YouTube limit can still be dismissed, so Loq In remains the primary enforcement layer.</string>
    <string name="in_app_youtube_native_limit_compact_title">Extra Shorts protection</string>
    <string name="in_app_youtube_native_limit_compact_summary">YouTube limit · 0 min recommended</string>
    <string name="in_app_youtube_native_limit_compact_action">Set up</string>
    <string name="in_app_youtube_native_limit_guide_title">YouTube Shorts feed limit</string>
    <string name="in_app_youtube_native_limit_guide_body">In YouTube, open Settings → Time management → Shorts feed limit and set it to 0 minutes. Keep Loq In’s Shorts rule enabled as the primary blocking layer. YouTube’s own limit is an additional layer and can still be dismissed.</string>
